000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, WEDNESDAY, OCTOBER 18, 2006\r\rMayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:31 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman, Maurer and Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Coroalles, Lysik, Peirce, Permaul, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Robert Yalda.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, to approve the agenda with the revision to the agreement in Item #7. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\r Mayor pro Tem Bozajian announced that the Calabasas Pumpkin Festival will be taking place on Sunday, October 22, 2006 at DeAnza Park. Mayor pro Tem Bozajian also announced that the USTA Men�s Challenger Tennis Tournament will be occurring at the Calabasas Tennis & Swim Center. He spoke regarding the annual Hidden Hills Parade in which he had participated during the previous weekend. Councilmember Maurer announced that the Calabasas 5K/10K Walk/Run will be happening on November 11, 2006. Mayor Washburn announced that the bids for the Civic Center Project were opened on October 18, 2006 at 2:00 p.m.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Pamela Evans, Calabasas, spoke regarding the cost of solar power permits in the City. Carl Olson, spoke in opposition to the City�s ban on secondhand smoke. \r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the September 27, 2006 and October 4, 2006 City Council meetings.\r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2006-229, making non-substantive changes to Title 3 of the Calabasas Municipal Code regarding the transient occupancy tax (hotel bed tax).\r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2006-230, making non-substantive changes to Title 3 of the Calabasas Municipal Code regarding refund claims.\r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2006-231, amending the Calabasas Municipal Code to clarify its original intent and to remove obsolete references in the telephone users tax section of the Calabasas Municipal Code.\r\r Recommendation to accept completion of the Annual Citywide Cape Seal project by Copp Contracting, specification no. 05-06-05; and to direct the City Clerk to file the Notice of Completion.\r\r Request approval of a service contract with Durham School Services to provide the City with supplemental public transportation resources; and authorize the City Manager to execute the contract.\r\r Authorization to execute a professional services agreement�with City Permit Services for as-needed processing of film permits. \r\r Recommendation from the Communications and Technology Commission to request the addition of an access channel to the City�s three cable franchises.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson to approve Items #1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 and 8 with revised language to the agreement in #7. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r CONTINUED PUBLIC HEARING � Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1014, establishing revised affordable housing in-lieu fees for residential development projects and a revised affordable housing impact fee for commercial development projects, in accordance with Chapter 17.22 of the Municipal Code.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Mayor Washburn opened the public hearing.\r\r Maureen Tamuri, Community Development Director and Tom Bartlett, City Planner, presented the staff report. \r\rThe City Council concurred to continue the item to the November 1, 2006 City Council meeting.\r\r CONTINUED PUBLIC HEARING � Waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2006-224, amending the User's Guide and Chapter 22, Affordable Housing, of Title 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code, as necessary to bring the City's Density Bonus provisions into conformance with the affordable housing laws of the State of California.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Mayor Washburn opened the public hearing.\r\r Maureen Tamuri, Community Development Director and Tom Bartlett, City Planner, presented the staff report. \r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to continue the item to the November 1, 2006 City Council meeting.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1052, approving an extension to the project time line in Resolution No. 2005-982, which approved a one-year extension to the project time line in Resolution No. 2000-629, vacating a certain portion of Driver Avenue between the west City limits and Parkville Road.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Mayor Washburn opened the public hearing.\r\r Mayor Washburn closed the public hearing.\r\rMayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, adopt Resolution No. 2006-1052, approving an extension to the project time line in Resolution No. 2005-982, which approved a one-year extension to the project time line in Resolution No. 2000-629, vacating a certain portion of Driver Avenue between the west City limits and Parkville Road. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1053, approving documents related to the issuance of the 2006 Certificates of Participation (City Hall and Civic Center Project) and the execution and delivery of the not to exceed $35,000,000 Certificates of Completion.\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, adopt Resolution No. 2006-1053, approving documents related to the issuance of the 2006 Certificates of Participation (City Hall and Civic Center Project) and the execution and delivery of the not to exceed $35,000,000 Certificates of Completion. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Discussion regarding City Council meeting schedule changes for December 2006 and January 2007.\r\rThe Council concurred to cancel the meetings of December 20, 2006 and January 3, 2007.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of September 28, 2006 to October 6, 2006.\r\rNo Action Taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r There were no task force reports.\r\rRECESSED TO CALABASAS FACILITIES CORPORATION BOARD OF DIRECTORS MEETING\r\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r The City Manager indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r The City Council requested that the Council appointment to the Santa Monica Conservancy Advisory Council and an update on Calabasas Road be placed on the next City Council agenda.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:17 p.m.\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 4 -\u0015\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u